            <ArticleTitle>Imaging of Mueller-Weiss Syndrome: A Review of Clinical Presentations and Imaging Spectrum.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>W8-W18</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.2214/AJR.15.15843</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">Mueller-Weiss syndrome is a complex condition of the adult tarsal navicular characterized by progressive fragmentation leading to mid- and hindfoot pain and deformity. Since its first descriptions in the early 20th century, controversy has persisted regarding its pathogenesis.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">This article reviews the literature and discusses the anatomy, epidemiology, causes, clinical and radiologic findings, and treatment of Mueller-Weiss syndrome, and thus permits a better understanding of this disease and its management.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
